## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/prefixsumcore.html
- Summary (EN): The Prefix Sum Core node computes a prefix sum by scanning the buffer of an input layer. Besides addition, it can produce running minimums, maximums, or counts of non-zero elements.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Prefix Sum Core est un ancien nœud de préfixe masqué et non supporté, à ne pas utiliser dans un nouveau travail.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer to compute the prefix sum from"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Operation: Add, Minimum, Maximum or Count Non-Zero", "Inclusive: when on, each prefix includes the current element; when off, the first element becomes the identity value of the operation"]

- Caveats: ["The node type is hidden and no longer supported; do not use it in new work.", "The Copernicus index lists a separate Prefix Sum node, which this page does not cover."]

